// Title: BITS Transfer Job With Uncommon Or Suspicious Remote TLD
// ID: 6d44fb93-e7d2-475c-9d3d-54c9c1e33427
// Status: test
// Level: medium
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-06-10
// Tags: attack.persistence, attack.execution, attack.stealth, attack.t1197
// Description: Detects a suspicious download using the BITS client from a FQDN that is unusual. Adversaries may abuse BITS jobs to persistently execute or clean up after malicious payloads.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((where(EventID = "16403")) AND NOT (((where(RemoteName ICONTAINS ".azureedge.net/") OR where(RemoteName ICONTAINS ".com/") OR where(RemoteName ICONTAINS ".sfx.ms/") OR where(RemoteName ICONTAINS "download.mozilla.org/") OR where(RemoteName ICONTAINS "cdn.onenote.net/") OR where(RemoteName ICONTAINS "cdn.office.net/") OR where(RemoteName ICONTAINS "tscdn.m365.static.microsoft/")))))
